TITLE:: ViewUnicode
SUMMARY:: Common unicode code points for the unicode argument of LINK::Classes/View:: keyboard actions.
CATEGORIES:: GUI
RELATED:: Classes/ViewKeyModifier, Classes/ViewQtKey, Classes/ViewKeycode, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter

DESCRIPTION::
The third argument to LINK::Classes/View:: CODE::keyDownAction:: / CODE::keyUpAction:: is the Unicode code point of the event text. For printable keys it usually equals CODE::char.ascii::. Special keys often use CODE::0::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: carriageReturn
Unicode code point 13 (carriage return); used by some Enter/Return chords alongside CODE::ViewQtKey.return::.

METHOD:: none
Zero; no text character (typical for arrow keys and Ctrl+letter when CODE::char:: is null).
